PROJECT: LIBRARY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

Description:
------------
Developed a console-based Library Management System to manage books, librarians, book issuing and returning, book availability, due dates, and fines.
The application allows library staff to add, display, search, issue, and return books while tracking issued books using a HashMap.
LocalDate is used for issue dates, due dates, fine calculation, and due-date reminders.

Main Classes:
--------------
• Book – Stores book details such as book ID, title, author, and availability.
• User – Stores user ID and user name.
• Librarian – Stores librarian ID and librarian name.
• LibraryService – Handles the main library operations such as adding books, searching, issuing, returning, fines, reminders, and reports.
• Library/Main – Provides the menu-driven console interface.

Features Implemented:
---------------------
• Add new books
• Display all books
• Search books by Book ID
• Search books by title
• Search books by author
• Check book availability
• Add librarians
• Verify librarian before issuing a book
• Get librarian approval before issuing a book
• Issue books to users
• Return issued books
• Track issued books using user ID
• Calculate fine for overdue books
• Fine is calculated at ₹10 per overdue day
• Collect fine and display payment status
• Calculate a 7-day due date from the issue date
• Provide due-date reminders
• Generate library reports
• Display total books, available books, issued books, and total librarians
• Display issued book details and due dates

